;
; DEVS:Internet/routes
;
; Where the default route lives: the address of the router that everything
; not on your own network gets handed to.
;
; This is the file Roadshow uses.  There is no DEVS:Internet/default_gateway
; in Roadshow 1.15, whatever secondary sources may say -- although
; AmiNetXDuo reads one if it finds it, because its own design notes called
; for it and a file that exists should not be ignored.
;
; WITH DHCP YOU DO NOT NEED THIS FILE.  The router's address arrives with the
; lease.
;

; DEFAULT -- the router.  Usually the address ending in .1 or .254 on your
; own network.  DEFAULTGATEWAY= is accepted as a synonym.
;
DEFAULT=192.168.1.1

; A route to one particular network, through some other gateway.  DST names
; the destination, VIA the gateway to reach it through.  NETDST and HOSTDST
; say explicitly whether the destination is a network or a single machine.
;
; AmiNetXDuo parses these and does not install them yet -- only the default
; route is acted on.
;
;DST=10.0.0.0    VIA=192.168.1.254
;HOSTDST=10.1.2.3 VIA=192.168.1.254
